Business Requirement:
For multiple applications sharing the same LINKED_APPLICATION_NUMBER, select one deterministic application record to avoid arbitrary results.

Test Performed:
Tested linked application groups with multiple application identifiers and different case statuses. Verified the prioritisation logic: COMPLETE first, then non-WITHDRAWN, and if all are WITHDRAWN select the latest application identifier.

Expected Result:
Only one application is selected per LINKED_APPLICATION_NUMBER and the same record is consistently selected on each run.

Actual Result:
Deduplication logic returned one deterministic record per linked application group as expected.

Evidence:
SQL test results showing multiple application identifiers under the same LINKED_APPLICATION_NUMBER and the selected record after applying the prioritisation logic.